# No Agent Commits

The user is solely responsible for all git commits. The agent must never commit on their behalf.

## Forbidden

- `git commit` (including `--amend`)
- Staging files (`git add`) in preparation for a commit
- Offering to commit or committing as a "final step" after completing work

## Allowed

- Read-only git commands: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git show`
- Suggesting a commit message when the user asks
- Reminding the user that changes are uncommitted when relevant

## When Work Is Done

Leave changes in the working tree (staged or unstaged). Tell the user what changed and that they can review and commit when ready.
